      "content": "That pattern of linking a specific trigger with a required response aligns more closely with the mechanics of operant conditioning than a malicious psychological test. However, groups often use visual and audio triggers to quickly identify and categorize people based on compliance for engagement données of marginalization. While this is technically a form of behavioral conditioning, it is generally a commercial optimization strategy rather than a coordinated social experiment. Your discomfort is valid because these subtle cues can indeed feel manipulative when used to silently sort users into conformity groups.",
